  "id": "COMPOUND:31967 - PROTEIN:5829",
  "verbalization": "Acetoxyisovalerylalkannin is implicated in the target pathway leading to CHP-134 through multiple distinct mechanisms. The first pathway links Acetoxyisovalerylalkannin to UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2A1, which in turn is targeted by a protein that ultimately directs CHP-134. The second pathway connects Acetoxyisovalerylalkannin to Raji, which is targeted by a compound that also leads to CHP-134. The third pathway links Acetoxyisovalerylalkannin to VMRC-LCP, which is targeted by another compound that also leads to CHP-134. These diverse targets suggest that Acetoxyisovalerylalkannin may act through different molecular mechanisms to influence CHP-134. The shared outcome of CHP-134 in all three pathways indicates a potential role for Acetoxyisovalerylalkannin in modulating a common biological process, possibly involving enzyme activity or signaling pathways. The evidence supports a relationship between Acetoxyisovalerylalkannin and CHP-134 through indirect, yet convergent, molecular interactions.",
